{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Let's pin down what this actually is before we talk stack. \"Personal finance stuff\" covers a lot — my read is you want a **budget/expense tracker**: you log transactions (or import them), sort them into categories, and see where your money goes. That's the most common core for a personal-finance site and it gives us a clean thing to build a foundation around. Does that match what's in your head, or are you picturing something else (e.g. investment/portfolio tracking, bill reminders, net-worth dashboard, savings goals)?","choices":["Budget/expense tracker (log & categorize spending)","Investment / portfolio tracking","Bill reminders & recurring payments","Net-worth / accounts dashboard","Savings goals","Something else"],"recommended":"Budget/expense tracker (log & categorize spending)"},"prd":"# Mission: Establish foundation for personal finance website\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** _(pending alignment)_\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- _(to be defined — running skeleton, working test runner, one thin vertical slice)_\n**Out of Scope:**\n- Building the actual product features (deferred to follow-on missions)\n**Constraints:**\n- _(stack to be recommended and confirmed)_"}

